{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1002667-infernal-pacts","id":1002667,"title":"Infernal Pacts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-13T15:46:12-08:00","id":1002667,"title":"Infernal Pacts","content":"So, I was thinking about the nature of Infernal Pacts. In Hedge Wizard, they divide Infernal Pacts into two level, Lesser and Greater, and they give concrete bonuses for each. A Lesser Pact gives 3 Path levels and 3 Rituals while a Greater Pact gives 5 Path levels and 6 Rituals. A Greater Pact, also known as a Soul Pact, also allows characters to gain access to Demonic Investments, from Book of Madness, by effectively borrowing against the soul that they have promised their patron (similar to a Reverse Mortgage).<br /> <br /> I think that the Infernal Lords would not discriminate and would be willing to offer power to anyone who contacts them (or is promising enough for them to contact). While the majority of the contact rituals require deprivity, I imagine they are window dressing and that an Infernal Lord would come if called by someone desperate enough to deal with them. I imagine that they would offer a Lesser Pact first with reasonable terms (3 Path levels and 3 Rituals in exchange for monthly worship) and would offer a Greater Pact after their minion has proven to be interesting enough. After the Greater Pact, they would be willing to negotiate Demonic Investments. I was wondering if anyone else played the Infernal Pacts like that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-13T16:54:43-08:00","id":1002700,"title":"","content":"By my part, I just used Pacts as in Demon the Fallen Core. The problem with Infernal Pacts is that there are more than half a dozen distinct rules to cover them, though I'm not sure if this is the problem for you.<br /> <br /> Your way of doing that seem good enough as a rule of thumb. What I would add, if you want to work demons to such extend, is the goals of the demon itself. It could change any of those practices by analyzing how the character in question could and would help the demon. Sometimes ignore the window dressing, or even try to appear as a good being. Sometimes it is worth to go full power on a mortal from the very beginning, because it will stir the character to the desired direction.<br /> <br /> And sometimes even demons go wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-13T17:21:48-08:00","id":1002712,"title":"","content":"Demonic dealings are a mess. The system for it changes in almost every book. Personally, I like 1000 hell's take, in which you give a list of things you want, all worth points, and you roll your law to see how much of a discount you get. You can get stuff for free. But then again, no book for western splats has yama kings in it. <br /> There's a system where you do sins ranked 1-10 for points for stuff. A solid XP system for stuff. <br /> Devils due has a single agreement where you become the devils servant in life and remove yourself from god's grace, but otherwise don't suffer anything so long as you serve with faith.<br /> <br /> <br /> Just go for XP costs which are reduced from what they'd normally be (Paths are X3, Dark Thaumaturgy is X4 or 6, Attributes are X3. Investments are whatever you think they're worth) <br /> <br /> Exchanging information or resources. Nothing needed, maybe some foul stuff. They can always try to get more than what they give. <br /> Changing the character positively- Part of the soul<br /> Changing the character enough- All of the soul. <br /> <br /> Sources give dark thaumaturgy as something you need to change all the soul for sometimes. Honestly, I think you could probably get it without damning yourself through taking a slower route than 'Instant magic' but instead taking the time to learn it, though I imagine demons are far happier to blast you into magical power at the price of more soul. <br /> <br /> But, it seems that nobody really wants to nail down demons, so it's really up to storyteller.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Signatures are for terrible people who want to be caught.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12414-flower-innocent","name":"Flower,Innocent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}